<p>
            <strong>For most runners the best fast treadmill is the Sole F83: 12 mph, a 22 by 60-inch
            deck, a 3.5 HP motor and a lifetime frame and motor warranty for about $1,700 on Amazon; if you
            need more than 12 mph, the STEPR Tread XL reaches 15.5 mph on a 63-inch deck.</strong>
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>12 mph</strong> is a 5:00 mile and is enough for tempo runs, fast intervals and strides for nearly everyone.</li>
            <li><strong>14 to 15.6 mph</strong> (4:17 to 3:51 a mile) is for sprinters and very fast runners. The <a href="/lifesmart-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>Lifesmart</a> TM4000C reaches 14 mph for about $1,199; the STEPR and GYMOST pass 15 mph.</li>
            <li><strong>Belt length</strong>: look for 60 inches or more for fast running. At 12 mph the belt moves about 211 inches a second, so small lapses move you a long way.</li>
            <li><strong>Motor</strong>: a continuous rating of 3 HP or more is the usual guide for regular running; a peak figure tells you less.</li>
            <li><strong>Speed changes</strong> matter as much as top speed for short reps. Only the 3G Cardio listing gives a figure: 0 to 12 mph in 18 seconds.</li>
          </ul>
