        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>What is the fastest treadmill on Amazon?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Of the named-brand listings we found on 21 November 2026, the GYMOST commercial treadmill lists the highest top speed at 15.6 mph, and the STEPR Tread XL lists 15.5 mph. The STEPR’s top speed is also confirmed by Rogue Fitness. Most home treadmills on Amazon stop at 10 or 12 mph.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is a 12 mph treadmill fast enough?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For nearly everyone, yes. Twelve mph is a five-minute mile, or a 75-second 400 metres, which covers tempo runs, intervals and strides for most runners. Sprinters and very fast middle-distance runners whose reps are quicker than that need 14 to 15 mph or a curved manual trainer.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is 15 mph on a treadmill in minutes per mile?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Fifteen mph is a four-minute mile, or about 2:29 per kilometre. Divide 60 by the speed in mph to get minutes per mile: 12 mph is 5:00 and 14 mph is about 4:17.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How long should a treadmill belt be for sprinting?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              At least 60 inches, and 62 or more if you are tall or will sprint above 12 mph often. At 12 mph the belt moves about 211 inches a second, so a short lapse in concentration moves you back a long way, and your stride is longer at speed. Decks of 55 inches suit jogging rather than fast running.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What horsepower do I need for a fast treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              A continuous rating of about 3 HP or more is the common guide for regular running, and more for heavier runners and frequent fast running. Check whether the figure is continuous or peak: a peak rating is a brief maximum and says less about holding 12 mph for a minute.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can you sprint on a treadmill without a fast top speed?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              You can raise the effort with incline instead of speed, and many sprint sessions use a few per cent of grade for that reason. It is a different stimulus from flat sprinting, though. If you need flat speed above 12 mph, buy a faster machine or a curved manual trainer.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
